SUMMARY:OutMontclair and Watchung Booksellers Award-Winning Storyteller Phill Branch
DESCRIPTION:Out Montclair and Watchung Booksellers kick off Pride month with Moth Grand-SLAM Storyteller and Emmy Award-winning director Phill Branch\, discussing his powerful memoir\, Double Dutch Fuss\, with former Black-Eyed Peas singer/songwriter Kim Hill on Wednesday\, June 3 at 7:00 p.m. \nIn this raw and lyrical memoir\, Branch chronicles his struggle to break free from—and live outside of—the prescribed paradigms of Blackness and masculinity that shaped him. Growing up\, Phill paid greatly for his failures at boyhood\, especially when he was caught playing jump rope with girls. This taught him there were standards to be met\, codes that were not to be violated\, and strict punishment for any deviation from a Black man’s assigned position in the world. \nBranch reckons with the patriarchy and tradition of these social structures in Black America and how healing wounds can open a pathway toward freedom and wholeness. \nTickets are $5 and include a 10% discount on the book at the event. Purchase at watchungbooksellers.com. \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
URL:https://montclairlocal.news/event/outmontclair-and-watchung-booksellers-award-winning-storyteller-phill-branch/
LOCATION:Watchung Booksellers\, 54 Fairfield Street\, Montclair\, NJ\, 97042\, United States
CATEGORIES:General Events
